{"id": "EUVD-2026-101218", "enisaUuid": "c1246782-2257-3ccd-a878-2ebdf068d23a", "description": "OW2 ASM 3.0 before 9.11 contains an uncontrolled memory allocation vulnerability in the asm-commons JSRInlinerAdapter that inlines JSR/RET subroutines without memory or work limits. Attackers can supply a crafted class file with nested subroutines to force O(2^n) memory allocation, causing an OutOfMemoryError that crashes the JVM.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:16:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T14:16:35", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://gitlab.ow2.org/asm/asm/-/merge_requests/466", "https://gitlab.ow2.org/asm/asm/-/commit/f2b988af48719f85a274f2a05e37bc55c0cd22a1", "https://gitlab.ow2.org/asm/asm/-/blob/ASM_9_10_1/asm-commons/src/main/java/org/objectweb/asm/commons/JSRInlinerAdapter.java#L232", "https://asm.ow2.io/versions.html", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ow2-asm-3.0-before-9.11-exponential-memory-allocation-in-jsrinlineradapter"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110270", "GHSA-53jq-h6qp-vprp"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a8295b77-0214-3921-8ab0-689de84a955b", "product": {"name": "ASM", "vendor": {"name": "OW2"}}, "product_version": "3.0 <9.11"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3926835e-88b8-36fa-aff5-949eba767278", "vendor": {"name": "OW2"}}], "isExploited": false}